Drop the manager rules that only the KairosControlPlane path uses, so a
platform that runs Kairos workers only does not grant the bootstrap manager
ServiceAccount tokens, Role and RoleBinding writes, or VMI reads.
In cluster-api-provider-kairos v0.2.1 the ManagementEndpointResolver creates
the ServiceAccount, its token, the Role (granting virtualmachineinstances get)
and the RoleBinding (internal/controllers/bootstrap/management_endpoint_resolver.go:143,160,219,234),
and render.go:216 calls it only for role == "control-plane". The startup
NodePushRoleMigrator lists Roles through mgr.GetAPIReader(), an uncached
reader (main.go:441, rbac_migrator.go:72), so list alone keeps that read; it
patches only node-push Roles, which the control-plane path creates. The
KairosConfig controller watches no Role, ServiceAccount or VMI
(kairosconfig_controller.go:1492-1518).

--- a/bootstrap-components-kairos.yaml
+++ b/bootstrap-components-kairos.yaml
@@ -2439,18 +2439,6 @@
   verbs:
   - create
   - delete
-  - get
-  - list
-  - patch
-  - update
-  - watch
-- apiGroups:
-  - ""
-  resources:
-  - serviceaccounts
-  - serviceaccounts/token
-  verbs:
-  - create
   - get
   - list
   - patch
@@ -2546,23 +2534,11 @@
   - list
   - watch
 - apiGroups:
-  - kubevirt.io
-  resources:
-  - virtualmachineinstances
-  verbs:
-  - get
-- apiGroups:
   - rbac.authorization.k8s.io
   resources:
-  - rolebindings
   - roles
   verbs:
-  - create
-  - get
   - list
-  - patch
-  - update
-  - watch
 ---
 apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
 kind: RoleBinding
